  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\[\\dfrac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}} ?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(2013\\)",
    "E": "\\(2^{4024}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The exponents differ by \\(2\\), so\n\\[\n2^{2014}=2^{2012}\\cdot 2^2=4\\cdot 2^{2012}.\n\\]\nThis lets us factor out the same large number from the numerator and denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}}\n=\\frac{2^{2012}(4+1)}{2^{2012}(4-1)}\n=\\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nThe cancellation is valid because \\(2^{2012}>0\\); the denominator is \\(3\\cdot 2^{2012}>0\\) as well. The value is \\(\\frac{5}{3}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
